{"title":"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Similar_Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Similar Problems</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a group of nine people each person shakes hands with exactly two of the other people from the group. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of ways this handshaking can occur. Consider two handshaking arrangements different if and only if at least two people who shake hands under one arrangement do not shake hands under the other arrangement. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given that each person shakes hands with two people, we can view all of these through graph theory as 'rings'.  This will split it into four cases:  Three rings of three, one ring of three and one ring of six, one ring of four and one ring of five, and one ring of nine. (All other cases that sum to nine won't work, since they have at least one 'ring' of two or fewer points, which doesn't satisfy the handshaking conditions of the problem.)\n</p><p><b>Case 1:</b>   To create our groups of three, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/1/da1937ab4b3248e36ed7bef3e40207fa9f3b7b75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\dbinom{9}{3}\\dbinom{6}{3}\\dbinom{3}{3}}{3!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"114\" height=\"73\" />.  In general, the number of ways we can arrange people within the rings to count properly is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/41764f96294d6b98e40ca553b5e4f68c19b4313c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{(n-1)!}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" />, since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c680399c425113bf35cf459f6690f834aa62ac47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-1)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> ways to arrange items in the circle, and then we don't want to want to consider reflections as separate entities.  Thus, each of the three cases has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa68cf0205f474f9d239c30057ddf96449d9d49c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{(3-1)!}{2}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"99\" height=\"40\" /> arrangements.  Therefore, for this case, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3ce101fa8dcd59ad34a86c39f1ee5ff0b5a411e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\dfrac{\\dbinom{9}{3}\\dbinom{6}{3}\\dbinom{3}{3}}{3!}\\right)(1)^3=280$\" style=\"vertical-align: -49px\" width=\"231\" height=\"109\" />\n</p><p><b>Case 2:</b>  For three and six, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/c/f8c49b416ae3f0df821aac3f999211eed7018e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{9}{6}=84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"79\" height=\"53\" /> sets for the rings.  For organization within the ring, as before, there is only one way (i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/9/c392de1fba338e11d011c5d6883a3e0eae6f134c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3-1)!/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" />)to arrange the ring of three.  For six, there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70df2da5f579b356990bb53e9ebd377272c0ed8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{(6-1)!}{2}=60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" />.  This means there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/0/eb0e2fc49d21583a4b661a3feab10579006db8b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(84)(1)(60)=5040$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" /> arrangements.\n</p><p><b>Case 3:</b>  For four and five, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/4/4849fdebae8208864ee7da22e4209901022ebcbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{9}{5}=126$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"88\" height=\"53\" /> sets for the rings.  Within the five, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/3/98307aeb4d00fd606292ec844f92610b53586daf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{4!}{2}=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"38\" />, and within the group of four there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/2/f72d2f5e47778d1b0ca14953ff0411b08cce7112.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{3!}{2}=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"51\" height=\"38\" /> arrangements.  This means the total is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b82cbbd35f03655840db3a817be8642a2ae44f98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(126)(12)(3)=4536$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><b>Case 4:</b>  For the nine case, there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/7/837c868aae7d634c62e67b0b89a39a6a482d3133.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{9}{9}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"69\" height=\"53\" /> arrangement for the ring.  Within it, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/3/22339fbf855dd86120f67ea3d93e0f0bc7aef580.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{8!}{2}=20160$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" /> arrangements.\n</p><p>Summing the cases, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/f/e6f6b168ce4b0574b04168dbc412323f02bbe74b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$280+5040+4536+20160=30016 \\to \\boxed{016}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"349\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Note: the reason why we divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/6859713adc973d3fbe97fafef9ce829757e54b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> in Case 1 and not the other three cases is because for case one and case one only, the groups each have 3 people, implying a symmetric configuration. \n</p><p>For example, for 3 people A, B, C in group 1, they could very well be in group 2 or 3 too, because each group has 3 people. \n</p><p>However, for all the other three cases, the configurations are not symmetric and so dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08ce4ccc8f0624befaa9ce7855fc1afc69b8e5ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> or like would be incorrect. It is not possible to configure A, B, C such that they can be both a group of 3 and a group of 6, since {A, B, C} only has 3 elements. \n</p><p>~mathboy282\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/c/afcc909ebe4cf02329d4d402b0d9decc228c3883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"18\" /> be the number of ways a group of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> people can shake hands with exactly two of the other people from the group, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/8/ca8db641f6d1f6ab5e24fd4004a8a31c4a8b59f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>We can easily find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/1/f11a507581268dc7f19b5c0faae3f7243fa3dadd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_3=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Continuing on, we will label the people as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,... corresponding with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/9/f3911668df13fa9062eeaa179db4af30856d5b9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"16\" />: There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/4/cf4e022244f58db56a34b172a29b1bd4f4c07155.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{3}{2}=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"70\" height=\"53\" /> possible ways for person <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to shake hands with two others (WLOG assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> shakes hands with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />), and there is only one possible outcome thereon (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> both shakes hands with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />).\n</p><p>Therefore, we can conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc1ac13b7ab5f166872551c88d3af6b9a7f6c78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_4=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/b/35b83c21f51407f81ea34a0ef014a4f629e1f9ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"16\" />: There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/8/218cac1c888eb03e613d452eb1c40f3466c75d77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{4}{2}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"70\" height=\"53\" /> possible ways for person <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to shake hands with two others (WLOG assume they are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />). Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> must also shake hands with the remaining two people (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways), and those last <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> people must shake hands with each other (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> way).\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/6/e0683cec2ce0a3f8f903de3f919015ba7af7eb30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_5=\\dbinom{4}{2}\\ast(2)\\ast(1)=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"203\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb3638a2de34dae8061ee8c62d93010abadc7c56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"16\" />: There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/6/e6653deb030534d3b1c16ff1b5f7a31885a56ea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{5}{2}=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"79\" height=\"53\" /> possible ways for person <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to shake hands with two others (WLOG assume they are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />). However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> shake hands with each other, then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/5/bf546afa0f53af4bfa4073696f82eef753b79edd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"16\" /> ways for the rest of the people to shake hands. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> shake hands with two others out of the three remaining people (3<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/278afa87a7dfa8e2b3f40e608884a690fb1325f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ast$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" />2 ways), those <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> people must shake hands with the last person (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> way).\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/9/609f79b4167088508af681f9c78df91fc41a6789.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_6=\\dbinom{5}{2}\\ast(f_3)+3\\ast(2)\\ast(1)=70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"282\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Now we have enough information to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04ab4c9f8bd774513fb4536f759fe4485fc5a463.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04ab4c9f8bd774513fb4536f759fe4485fc5a463.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"16\" />: There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/4/0f412d7dfa35f127e374a26ba79ed7dc9391c250.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{8}{2}=28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"79\" height=\"53\" /> possible ways for person <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to shake hands with two others (WLOG assume they are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />).\n</p><p><b>Case 1:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> shake hands with each other\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb3638a2de34dae8061ee8c62d93010abadc7c56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"16\" /> ways for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to shake hands\n</p><p><b>Case 2:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> shake hands with one of the others out of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> remaining people (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways)\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/b/35b83c21f51407f81ea34a0ef014a4f629e1f9ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"16\" /> ways for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to shake hands\n</p><p><b>Case 3:</b> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> shake hands with two different people (there are 6<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/278afa87a7dfa8e2b3f40e608884a690fb1325f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ast$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" />5 ways to choose the people but WLOG assume they are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />). Calculations of Case 3 are in its subcases.\n</p><p><b>Subcase 3.1:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> shake hands with each other\nThere are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/9/f3911668df13fa9062eeaa179db4af30856d5b9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"16\" /> ways for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to shake hands\n</p><p><b>Subcase 3.2:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> each shake hands with one other person (there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to choose the person, WLOG let that be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />)\nThere are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/5/bf546afa0f53af4bfa4073696f82eef753b79edd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"16\" /> ways for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to shake hands\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Subcase 3.3:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> each shake hands with two different people (there are 4<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/278afa87a7dfa8e2b3f40e608884a690fb1325f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ast$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" />3 ways, WLOG let that be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />)\nThere are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88bd45254bab369c248f52b079447f0dc2fea401.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\ast1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" /> ways for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to then shake hands with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> will shake hands with each other.\n</p><p>We have \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d5d6608fa9c86a93f796a019648532f481e433.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 28(f_6+6\\ast(f_5)+6\\ast(5)\\ast(f_4)+4\\ast(f_3)+4\\ast(3)\\ast(2)\\ast(1) &amp;= 28(70+6\\ast(12)+6\\ast(5)\\ast(3+4\\ast(1)+4\\ast(3)\\ast(2)\\ast(1) \\\\ &amp;= 30016 \\end{align*}\" width=\"947\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>which gives us the answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/9/8d9da847dc164c20541513495aba09b2d917a666.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{016}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Daniel_Zhou%27s_Profile&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Daniel Zhou&#39;s Profile (page does not exist)\">Danielzh</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Very Neat solution: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lG8N9RuI-8o\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lG8N9RuI-8o</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Similar_Problems\">Similar Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Similar Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>2006 HMMT feb. combo #9.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h